30,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The bin house was actually kind of gross! It smelled really sour in the summer, and the next lane's supervised mornings only take about fifty minutes.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I found out that the ward subsidy covers forty percent up to ninety thousand yen, but last year's shelters averaged about two hundred forty-eight thousand yen. Also, we spend thirty-four thousand yen annually on maintenance.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"The complaint log is a mess; fourteen complaints in three years, and almost all of them came from the person living right next to the bins. The station block's minutes show they fought over a broken latch and sweeping duties.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"The truck arrives between 7:40 and 8:15, which is way too early for some. Plus, at the meeting, people admitted they wouldn't actually stop a neighbor from leaving a bag late.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The filing requirements are strict; a permanent build needs a site plan and four months, while every site change requires a new notice. Also, two frontages fit a bay, but one is a driveway and another is very narrow.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, so the bin house smells bad and the supervised mornings are short? Maybe we can just do the short mornings and avoid the smelly house!","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried about the cost of a shelter, though. Even with the subsidy, it's a lot of money upfront, and we're already spending thirty-four thousand yen a year just on basics.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, the ""short mornings"" might just lead to the same fighting the station block had over sweeping. And @Asuka, it sounds like moving the point around would be a bureaucratic nightmare.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Rin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. And if people won't even turn away a late bag, then ""supervised mornings"" are just a fancy way of saying one person stands there feeling awkward while everyone ignores them.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,It is also clear that rotating the location is physically impractical given the driveway and the narrow pavement of some frontages. We cannot simply move the point without creating new obstacles.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we don't move it, the person who complained so much will still be sad! @Shunichi, is there any way to make them happy without a smelly house?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"Maybe we can find a way to share the costs of a better setup so it doesn't feel like such a burden on one person, but the upfront price is still scary.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"The problem isn't just the money, Midori; it's the resentment. If we keep it where it is, that one neighbor keeps suffering, but if we move it, we might just move the anger to someone else.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"And if we go with a rotation, we're just rotating the stress. @Asuka, if the space is that limited, wouldn't a permanent structure just block the sidewalk for everyone?","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"Depending on the exact placement, it could. However, a permanent structure at the current site would at least avoid the need for constant notifications to the ward, which is a significant administrative burden.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I don't want anyone to be sad or angry! If the bin house smells and the rotation is a nightmare, maybe we can just find a way to make the current spot nicer?","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I agree with Rin. If we can find a way to make the current spot more manageable without spending too much, it might be the most harmonious choice for everyone.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"The problem is that ""making it nicer"" usually means spending money or time, and we've already seen that both of those things tend to lead to arguments. We need a solution that doesn't create new grudges.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm with Shunichi. If we just ""make it nicer"" without a real system, the same person will end up doing all the work and the same person will keep complaining. We need something that actually works.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,We must be realistic. The data shows that rotating the location is physically impossible for some and administratively tedious. We are left with either a strict time window or a permanent structure.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,May,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Rin,,I think the permanent house is a bad idea because of the smell! I'd rather just help out for fifty minutes in the morning. I vote for Option A!,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I'm worried about the high cost of the structure, and the maintenance fees are already a burden. I think Option A is safer for our budgets. I vote for Option A!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"I'm wary of the conflict a structure brings, and rotation is a mess. A time window is a risk, but it's the least permanent mistake. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"I'm not thrilled about the early hours or the lack of enforcement, but a permanent build is too much work and rotation is a joke. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"While Option A has flaws, the physical constraints of the frontages and the administrative burden of rotation make them unviable. A structure is too risky. I vote for Option A.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Rin,,Yay! We all agree! I'm glad we're picking the one that doesn't smell like old socks!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,I'm just relieved we found a way that doesn't put a huge financial strain on anyone. It feels like the most balanced choice for our group.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,Let's just hope we can actually agree on the turn order without it turning into another block war. I'll be watching closely.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"I'll be watching too. If I'm the only one answering the phone when things go wrong, I'm retiring from this committee immediately.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"We will establish a clear, written schedule for the oversight turns to ensure the burden is distributed logically and transparently.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I'll help make the schedule colorful so it's fun to look at! @Asuka, can I use my markers to make it pretty?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"That sounds lovely, Rin. A colorful schedule might make the whole process feel more positive for everyone involved.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Just make sure the dates are actually readable, Rin. We don't need a ""pretty"" schedule that leads to more arguments because someone couldn't tell if it was Tuesday or Wednesday.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shunichi, you're such a pessimist. I'm sure we can handle a few markers without starting a war, as long as the rules are crystal clear.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I will handle the drafting of the rules and the layout of the dates. Rin, you may add the colors once the logical structure is finalized and approved by everyone.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Rin,,"Okay! I'll wait for Asuka to finish the boring part, and then I'll make it the best-looking schedule ever!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,I'm just glad we could all reach an agreement together. I'll make sure to bring some tea and snacks for our next meeting to keep the mood light!,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,Tea and snacks might actually be the only thing keeping us from killing each other over a trash schedule. I'll be there.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"Count me in for the snacks too. If we're going to be standing on the street at 7:40 AM, I'm going to need a lot of caffeine to survive it.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,Then it is settled. I will prepare the draft for the ward office and the schedule for our review. Thank you all for your cooperation.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
